  "prompt_text": "Continue the text below with exactly one short, natural, coherent English sentence. Return only the continuation, with no preamble or explanation:\nWhen you're 28, science discovers a drug that stops all effects of aging, creating immortality. Your government decides to give the drug to all citizens under 26, but you and the rest of the “Lost Generations\" are deemed too high-risk. When you're 85, the side effects are finally discovered.\n\nYou didn't know what to think. It was like the world had just turned upside down in an instant. After all of these years, all of the tests and reports, they had finally found something wrong with the drug. But you couldn't help but feel like there was more to it. Why had it taken so long for side effects to show up? And why were they affecting both people who had taken the drug nearly 50 years ago and those who had taken it less than 10 years ago. At the same time? It didn't make sense to you. \n\nYou were still trying to figure it out when you got the call. An old friend of yours - well, weren't they all old now? - called you up and asked you to meet with her. \"Don't tell anyone\" she said. And you didn't.\n\nYou met her at an old restaurant, one stilled owned by another of the Lost Generations. \"I need to tell you something.\" she said. \"It's probably going to be hard to hear.\" She took a deep breath and looked at you, the wrinkles on her face deep with concern. \"These side effects aren't side effects of the drug. They are 'side effects' of government policy.\"\n\n\"What!\" \n\n\"Shhh\" she said. \"You must remain calm. We're can't take any risks right now.\" \n\n\"What are you talking about?\" you tried to remain calm, but judging by her face it was not a good performance. \n\n\"The side effects are the result of policy.",
  "reference_single_token_nfa_states": 20,
  "reference_text": " Think about it, if everyone lives forever the planet can't sustain us all for long. So when the population reaches a certain point, they hold a lottery.\" She covered her mouth after she said it, as if there was a possibility one of the other patrons would hear.\n\nOh god, you suddenly understood.",
